From a8b273e2972e2bcb4c8a63099c5ff1f4d2ccf570 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iimmyy <i.a.martins001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 08:05:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/34] ggml-cpu: add q2_K_8x4 repack for dotprod-only ARM
 cores

Adds a q2_K 8x4 interleave with NEON gemv/gemm kernels for CPUs with
dotprod but no i8mm (e.g. Cortex-A78/A55). The gemm decodes each
super-block's scales once and reuses them across rows (lane-indexed
vdotq_laneq_s32); the gemv applies per-pouch scales to raw int32 sums.
Generic reference kernels are written from the format definition, and
LG_Q2K_REFERENCE=1|gemv|gemm swaps them in for checking.
Measured on a QCS6490: pure Q2_K decode +31% vs Q4_0.
